  "summary": "The Marin County Sheriff's Office acknowledged that out-of-state and federal agencies accessed data from its 31 Flock cameras for nine weeks without permission in late 2024, conducting more than 250,000 searches as revealed by the Point Reyes Light newspaper. The ACLU and EFF have demanded answers, and a prior plaintiff is considering another lawsuit.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "multiple out-of-state agencies conducted more than 250,000 searches of Marin County's camera data in late 2024",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "upon discovering the issue, we again immediately deactivated the ability for out-of-state agencies to view our limited data.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "It is a menace to the safety of California residents for the Marin sheriff to be violating state law and letting license plate reader data leave our state and go to federal and out of state police departments",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    }
  ],
